<div class="mb-4">
  <h3 class="mb-0">Import Logs</h3>
  <div class="text-secondary small">Upload real log files. Events go through the same parser, detection engine and risk scoring as everything else.</div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3"><div class="card-body">
  <form id="ingestForm">
    <div class="row g-3">
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <label class="form-label small text-secondary">Log format</label>
        <select id="logFormat" class="form-select">
          <option value="auto">Auto-detect</option>
          <option value="auth">Linux auth.log / secure (SSH, sudo)</option>
          <option value="access">Web access log (Apache / Nginx)</option>
          <option value="csv">CSV (with header row)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-8">
        <label class="form-label small text-secondary">Log file (max ~1.5 MB)</label>
        <input id="logFile" type="file" class="form-control" accept=".log,.txt,.csv,text/plain,text/csv">
      </div>
      <div class="col-12">
        <label class="form-label small text-secondary">...or paste log lines</label>
        <textarea id="logText" class="form-control font-monospace" rows="8" placeholder="Nov  3 02:14:07 web01 sshd[811]: Failed password for root from 203.0.113.45 port 51522 ssh2"></textarea>
      </div>
    </div>
    <button id="ingestBtn" class="btn btn-danger mt-3" type="submit"><i class="bi bi-upload me-1"></i>Import &amp; Analyse</button>
  </form>
  <div id="ingestStatus" class="alert mt-3 d-none"></div>
</div></div>

<div class="row g-3">
  <div class="col-md-6"><div class="card h-100"><div class="card-body">
    <h6 class="text-secondary text-uppercase small mb-3">Try it with sample files</h6>
    <ul class="small mb-0">
      <li><a href="/samples/sample-auth.log" download>sample-auth.log</a> &mdash; SSH brute force, password spraying, off-hours login</li>
      <li><a href="/samples/sample-access.log" download>sample-access.log</a> &mdash; SQL injection, path traversal, scanner</li>
      <li><a href="/samples/sample-events.csv" download>sample-events.csv</a> &mdash; impossible travel</li>
    </ul>
  </div></div></div>
  <div class="col-md-6"><div class="card h-100"><div class="card-body">
    <h6 class="text-secondary text-uppercase small mb-3">What gets imported</h6>
    <div class="small text-secondary">Only security-relevant lines are stored (failed/successful logins, sudo abuse, malicious web requests, HTTP 401s). Normal traffic is ignored so the database stays small. Max 2000 events per upload.</div>
  </div></div></div>
</div>
